"} "Boglárka Kapás"] " and the United States’ " [:a {:href "/athletes/147282"} "Regan Smith"] ". Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/103469"} "Katinka Hosszú"] " had probably been the world’s best all-around swimmer in the last few years but struggled in Tokyo and never swam to her potential. She withdrew from this event, which led to a strange situation as there were only 17 entrants, and with Hosszú’s withdrawal, the preliminary round was meaningless as all 16 swimmers advanced to the semi-finals."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Zhang was the class of the event, posting the fastest times in both the preliminary round and her semi-final. In the final she went out quickly and poured it on, finishing in an Olympic record 2:03.86, 1.44 seconds ahead of Regan Smith, who took silver. Behind her Flickinger took bronze, comfortably ahead of Kapás."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This was Zhang’s second butterfly medal in Tokyo, adding to the silver she won in the 100 fly. She would add a gold in the 4 x 200 free relay and a silver in the mixed medley relay to go home with four medals, two of them gold. Smith also won a silver in the 100 backstroke and would win bronze in the 4 x 100 medley relay, while Flickinger added a second bronze medal in the 400 individual medley."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/129678"} "Zhang Yufei"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "2:07.50 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "2:04.89 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "2:03.86 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147282"} "Regan Smith"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img